# Template for electron-builder.env — copy it and fill in the blanks:
#
#     cp electron-builder.env.example electron-builder.env      (macOS / Git Bash)
#     copy electron-builder.env.example electron-builder.env    (Windows cmd)
#
# electron-builder loads electron-builder.env from the project root by itself
# (electron-builder/out/cli/cli.js -> loadEnv). That file is GITIGNORED and is not
# part of the repo, so each machine needs its own copy. Never commit real values.
#
# Only `npm run release:win` / `release:mac` need any of this. Plain `build:*`
# runs offline and needs none of it.


# ── Both platforms ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploads the release to github.com/terranivium/vocal-slice.
#
# Prefer a FINE-GRAINED personal access token limited to that one repository,
# with "Contents: Read and write" — enough to create a release and attach assets.
# A classic token with `public_repo` also works, but grants write access to every
# public repo you own, which is more than releasing needs.
#
# Fine-grained tokens expire. If a release suddenly fails with a 401 months from
# now, check the expiry date before anything else.
GH_TOKEN=


# ── macOS only (notarization) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these out on Windows — nothing there uses them.
#
# The signing CERTIFICATE is not configured here: it comes from the login keychain
# via `build.mac.identity` in package.json. So no CSC_* variables belong in this
# file. These three are only for submitting the build to Apple's notary service.
#
#   APPLE_ID                     the Apple Developer account email
#   APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD  appleid.apple.com -> Sign-In and Security ->
#                                App-Specific Passwords. NOT your Apple password.
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID                developer.apple.com -> Membership
APPLE_ID=
APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
